- `timer = null` is assigned immediately after scheduling, so the timer is effectively cleared before the next call. This means multiple invocations of the debounced function each schedule a new timer, and fn gets called multiple times with different arguments.
- Also, the early-return check `if (timer !== null) return` is essentially never true in practice (since timer is set to null synchronously), so it doesn't actually cancel and reschedule.

